    "body": "> As an example, `http://[::1%32]/` is currently failure per the URL Standard (and Gecko & WebKit), but `http://[::12]/` in Chromium. After the proposed change it would be `http://[[::1]/`. I'd rather align on failure.\r\n\r\nThis seems like a bug in Chromium. They shouldn't be doing percent decoding before invoking the IPv6 parser.",
